From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vlad Zahorodnii
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 12:09:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] wayland: Remove current extension state in
 SurfaceInterface::removeExtension as well

The idea was to preserve the current state, that the destructor request
doesn't affect the current state. On the other hand, the relevant
extension object will be gone, so that state cannot be accessed.

It should also fix SurfaceState::mergeInto() creating an incompatible
state object if a destroyed and a newly created RawSurfaceExtension
objects have the same address.

BUG: 510116


(cherry picked from commit 8931793d02ea497d610bd6cb4ccb864ccdfc82b7)

Co-authored-by: Vlad Zahorodnii

Carried unchanged: removeExtension is not touched by any Sparky Stereo patch, the hunk applies with a one-line offset. It is the fix of a KWin crash (BUG 510116): a surface extension
destroyed and a new one created at the same address gave SurfaceState::mergeInto() a state of the wrong type.

Origin: upstream, https://invent.kde.org/plasma/kwin/-/commit/5f587fb72b5dceaef911aa1ae848afb24f90be6a
Author: Vlad Zahorodnii
Applied-Upstream: v6.7.6, 5f587fb72b (Plasma/6.7), 8931793d02 (master); BUG 510116
Last-Update: 2026-11-07

Assisted-by: Claude Sonnet 5.5 via Claude Code
---
 src/wayland/surface.cpp | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/src/wayland/surface.cpp b/src/wayland/surface.cpp
index a647c9bb58..2a347b4f33 100644
--- a/src/wayland/surface.cpp
+++ b/src/wayland/surface.cpp
@@ -500,6 +500,7 @@ RawSurfaceAttachedState *SurfaceInterface::addExtension(RawSurfaceExtension *ext
 
 void SurfaceInterface::removeExtension(RawSurfaceExtension *extension)
 {
+    d->current->extensions.erase(extension);
     d->pending->extensions.erase(extension);
 
     if (d->subsurface.transaction) {
